# Documentation after implement (mandatory)

After **behavioral** implementation is done on a feature branch (logic in place; tests run per [testing-discipline.mdc](testing-discipline.mdc); [code-commenter pass](code-commenter-after-implement.mdc) when `src/` / `include/` changed), run a **documentation pass** before opening a draft PR or ending the implementation handoff.

## Required step

1. **Inventory** the full branch diff vs `main` for change signals (`src/`, `include/`, tests, Makefile, `.cursor/`, etc.). **Edit** only documentation paths (`docs/`, `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, `DEV_PLAN.md`, `.cursor/`) per the skill.
2. Delegate to the **docs-steward** subagent ([`docs-steward.md`](../agents/docs-steward.md)) or follow [documentation-maintainer skill](../skills/documentation-maintainer/SKILL.md).
3. Commit documentation updates on the same feature branch when the pass adds or fixes material worth keeping.
4. For milestone-tracked issues: use [milestone-issue-hygiene](../skills/milestone-issue-hygiene/SKILL.md) when creating/grooming; use [audit-github-devplan](../skills/audit-github-devplan/SKILL.md) only when auditing (fix with user approval).

## Skip when

- Change is comment-only in `src/` with no doc/workflow impact and user confirms skip
- User explicitly skips the documentation pass
- The same branch diff already had a documentation pass this session

## Workflow order

```text
implement → make test (and related targets) → code-commenter pass (if src/ or include/ touched) → documentation pass → draft PR
```

See [agent-workflow.mdc](agent-workflow.mdc) for PR and GitHub steps.
